ccess, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical: same status codes, same response bodies. Important: original success response: Content-Type set after possible errors? For errors, no Content-Type set. Body exactly {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no newline. 404 {\"error\":\"not found\"}, 500 {\"error\":\"db\"}. Success: json.Encoder.Encode adds trailing newline. Map order? Go map marshaling sorts keys alphabetically: email then name. So body: {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal(map[string]string{...}) and w.Write, no trailing newline, behavior changes. Need use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode or write with newline. But if we separate JSON encoding into function, can return bytes? If return bytes from json.Marshal, no newline. Could return bytes with newline? But \"JSON encoding\" function maybe encodeUserResponse(w, user) uses json.NewEncoder(w", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0026298740413039923], [760, -6.9340434074401855]], [[1144, -1.0371261851105373e-05], [14235, -12.127243995666504]], [[4087, -0.010717096738517284], [310, -4.749680995941162]], [[1156, -0.038186557590961456], [303, -3.5422472953796387]], [[579, -0.24398928880691528], [25, -2.286881685256958]], [[1622, -0.0032884846441447735], [3296, -6.628141403198242]], [[13, -0.3683154582977295], [25, -1.5728634595870972]], [[14235, -0.04048760235309601], [1165, -3.864271402359009]], [[89109, -0.32688575983047485], [7936, -1.815743088722229]], [[5805, -0.00025317296967841685], [2400, -8.653306007385254]], [[9830, -0.027313992381095886], [6795, -3.668055295944214]], [[6795, -2.908749047492165e-05], [17369, -11.931953430175781]], [[1083, -1.4061815738677979], [47781, -1.572572946548462]], [[1228, -0.09478510916233063], [2400, -2.823066234588623]], [[470, -3.433286474319175e-05], [5568, -10.547096252441406]], [[5568, -0.003063897369429469], [74243, -6.122376441955566]], [[440, -0.8858219981193542], [25, -1.877933144569397